{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && printf '\\\\n--- PACKET ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' lean/finite_fibers/aristotle_tasks/FF17-full-pauli-stabilizer-density.md && printf '\\\\n--- HANDOFF ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' lean/finite_fibers/HANDOFF.md && printf '\\\\n--- INVESTIGATION HANDOFF ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/HANDOFF.md && printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY MATCHES ---\\\\n' && rg -n -i -C 2 'finite_fiber|fullpauli|FF17|Aristotle|full pauli' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && printf '\\\\n--- PACKET ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' lean/finite_fibers/aristotle_tasks/FF17-full-pauli-stabilizer-density.md && printf '\\\\n--- HANDOFF ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' lean/finite_fibers/HANDOFF.md && printf '\\\\n--- INVESTIGATION HANDOFF ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/HANDOFF.md && printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY MATCHES ---\\\\n' && rg -n -i -C 2 'finite_fiber|fullpauli|FF17|Aristotle|full pauli' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\n\n--- PACKET ---\n# FF17 — actual finite stabilizer densities from full Pauli words\n\nRead `manuscript/main.tex` and work only in `formalization_finite_fibers`.\n\nCreate only `FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean`. Using FF15--FF16,\nconnect an explicitly finite consistent subgroup of `FullPauliWord Site` to\nits finite-region matrix image. Prove that the group average is the same\npositive trace-one stabilizer density already constructed abstractly in the\nfinite-density layer, with the exact sign/central-phase convention preserved.\nState all realization, consistency, and finite-support assumptions explicitly.\n\nDo not infer a countable stabilizer system from short-range order, and do not\nclaim a quasilocal state or GNS result. No placeholders or new axioms.\n\nAcceptance: `lake build FiniteFiber.FullPauliStabilizerDensity` succeeds; the\nresponse distinguishes the checked finite density identity from all global\nclaims.\n\n--- HANDOFF ---\n# Handoff: finite-fiber support-corner formalization\n\n## Read order\n\n1. `AGENTS.md` for scope and prohibition of historical dependencies.\n2. The canonical informal theorem note:\n   `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I001-full-tracial-corner/technical.tex`.\n3. `FiniteFiber/Basic.lean`.\n4. `FiniteFiber/TracialCorner.lean`.\n5. `FiniteFiber/FiniteFibers.lean`.\n6. `FiniteFiber/FiniteStabilizer.lean`.\n7. `FiniteFiber/FiniteStabilizerTrace.lean`.\n8. `FiniteFiber/FinitePauli.lean`.\n9. `FiniteFiber/FiniteQubitMatrix.lean`.\n10. `FiniteFiber/FiniteDensity.lean`.\n11. `FiniteFiber/FinitePauliStabilizer.lean`.\n12. `FiniteFiber/FiniteLocalPauli.lean`.\n13. `FiniteFiber/FiniteNestedPauli.lean`.\n14. `FiniteFiber/FiniteLocalGroupSupport.lean`.\n15. `FiniteFiber/ProjectivePauliLattice.lean`.\n16. `FiniteFiber/FullPauliLattice.lean`.\n17. `FiniteFiber/FiniteTensorMatrixChain.lean`.\n18. `FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionQubitAlgebra.lean`.\n19. `FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionPauliMatrices.lean`.\n20. `FiniteFiber/OneSitePauliNormalForm.lean`.\n21. `FiniteFiber/FiniteNestedTensorState.lean`.\n22. `FiniteFiber/FiniteStabilizerStateChain.lean`.\n23. `FiniteFiber/SequentialLocalFunctional.lean`.\n24. `FiniteFiber/StrongSupport.lean`.\n25. `FiniteFiber/StabilizerSequence.lean`.\n26. `FiniteFiber/VectorCorner.lean`.\n27. `FiniteFiber/GNSVector.lean`.\n28. `FiniteFiber/FinitePauliGNS.lean`.\n29. `FiniteFiber/GNSOrbit.lean`.\n30. `FiniteFiber/StabilizerFiniteFiber.lean`.\n\n## Mathematical contract\n\nThe primary formal theorem must prove the current manuscript's abstract\nconclusion:\n\n```text\nFor every nonzero central projection z of M,\nzM contains a nonzero finite projection.\n```\n\nIt is stronger than the finite-fiber corollary.  The theorem must not claim a\ndirect-integral decomposition or a type classification theorem.  The\nfinite-fiber corollary is obtained by applying it to explicitly supplied\ncentral projections indexed by a finite type.\n\n## Current proof architecture\n\n`Basic.lean` deliberately models finite projections through the standard\nMurray--von Neumann equations in a concrete von Neumann algebra and proves the\nderived partial-isometry identity needed by the corner argument.\n`TracialCorner.lean` uses a complex-linear functional that is tracial only\nwhen both arguments are supported in the corner, together with faithfulness on\nprojections below the corner support; this is exactly what is needed to prove\nfiniteness without introducing unnecessary normality machinery.\n`FiniteFibers.lean` combines that with the explicit fullness condition\n\n```text\nforall nonzero central z, z * q != 0.\n```\n\nThe checked nested-stabilizer-sequence application takes a finite self-adjoint\ngroup action, a supplied increasing finite subgroup sequence, and the\nremaining specified GNS-orbit data.  From those inputs it establishes:\n\n1. each local group average is a projection in the regional algebra and nested\n   subgroups make those supports decrease; their canonical strong limit `q`\n   lies in the regional algebra, is a projection, and fixes the GNS vector;\n2. the compressed vector functional is faithful on projections below the\n   corner support, using the dense product orbit and corner traciality;\n3. `q` is full using the same global GNS-density argument.\n\nThe single canonical entry point for those bundled clauses is\n`stabilizerAverageSequence_canonicalSupportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit`.  Its\n`q_projection`, `q_fixes_xi`, `full`, `projection_faithful`, and\n`central_witness` fields are the exact checked conclusions; `semifinite` is\ntheir existential central-summand corollary.  The separate\n`stabilizerAverageSequence_canonicalCentralWitness_of_gnsOrbit` declaration\nsupplies the canonical witness in a nonzero central summand.\n\n`FiniteStabilizerTrace.lean` separately proves the local finite-dimensional\ncalculation under the exact hypotheses that every nonidentity represented\ngroup element is traceless and `Module.finrank ℂ H ≠ 0`.  It is not used to\nestablish a nonzero global GNS support in the theorem above.\n\n`GNSVector.lean` supplements mathlib's generic GNS construction: for any\nsupplied positive linear functional on a unital C-star algebra, the image of\nthe unit has dense represented-algebra orbit and reconstructs the functional\nas a vector coefficient.  When the functional sends the unit to one, that\nvector has norm one; the vector is fixed whenever the supplied squared\ndeviation has zero functional value.  `FinitePauliGNS.lean` applies that\ncriterion to the finite stabilizer density and proves finite stabilizer\ninvariance of its own GNS vector.  These modules do not construct the\nmanuscript's quasi-local functional or establish a regional/complementary\nproduct-orbit density statement.\n\nI003 constructs the fixed finite ordered-qubit realization: explicit Hermitian\nsigned Pauli strings, finite group averages, trace-normalized positive density\nmatrices, and finite code-corner traciality.  Separately, it proves signed\npartial trace for normalized signed-Pauli expressions under the exact survivor\nequality; it does not manufacture that equality from trace orthogonality or\nassert that arbitrary signed expressions are states.  `FiniteNestedPauli.lean`\nthen lifts that calculation to actual finite larger and smaller stabilizer\ngroups, conditional on their explicit tensor-coordinate decomposition,\ninjective inclusion, and survivor iff.  It proves that the reindexed larger\ndensity is positive and trace-one and that its partial trace is the actual\nsmaller density.  `FiniteLocalGroupSupport.lean` derives the inclusion and\nsurvivor clauses from a supplied finite-support map and a supplied condition\nthat discarded identity labels detect support containment.  It does not\nconstruct that support map, the local algebras, or the Pauli-coordinate facts\nfrom a countable lattice.\n\n`ProjectivePauliLattice.lean` and `FullPauliLattice.lean` now construct the\nfinite-support projective and full normal-form Pauli groups.  The latter also\nderives the algebraic consistent stabilizer subgroup from an actual set of\npairwise-commuting order-two generators together with the consistency\ncondition excluding $-1$, and supplies the Pauli-label support predicate used\nto derive discarded-label survival for an explicitly enumerated finite\ncomplement.  This remains an algebraic normal-form result: its labels discard\nthe central `ZMod 4` phase, and no matrix realization or identification of\nsyntactic support with membership in a local matrix algebra is asserted.\n\n`FiniteQubitMatrix.lean` exposes the neutral finite-qubit operator-norm\nC-star scope.  `FiniteTensorMatrixChain.lean` constructs both a legacy\nrecursive tail-block coordinate convention and a checked literal\ninitial/final `Fin`-coordinate split.  It now proves that actual Hermitian\nsigned Pauli strings factor in those physical coordinates and that embedding\na string extends it by identity labels on the added block.\n`FiniteRegionQubitAlgebra.lean` bridges the abstract finite-region lattice\nlayer to actual finite matrix algebras: its `finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F` is\nthe matrix algebra on bit assignments `F \\to \\mathrm{Fin}\\,2`, and for each\n`F \\subseteq F'` its checked `finiteRegionEmbed` is the reindexed\n`A \\mapsto A \\otimes 1` inclusion.  The operator-norm structure is exported\nonly through `open scoped FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionQubitMatrix`; this fixes the\nprevious candidate-only local-instance limitation.  It remains independent of\nthe full Pauli/stabilizer matrix realization and has no multi-region\ncoherence, colimit, state, or GNS claim.\n`FiniteNestedTensorState.lean` uses this to derive the tensor decomposition\nof literal-coordinate nested stabilizer data, then proves its finite-density\nand state compatibility.  `FiniteStabilizerStateChain.lean` defines longer\ntransitions by `Nat.leRecOn` from physical one-site inclusions.  It proves\ntheir identity and composition laws at the typed endpoints, preserves the\nunital star-algebra structure and the finite operator norm, and proves\ninjectivity; the resulting linear maps are a checked `DirectedSystem`.  A\nstepwise compatible family of actual\nfinite stabilizer densities restricts along every such transition.  Its\nendpoint-to-added-block theorem identifies the maps with the original\nlength-indexed recursion and transfers the checked signed-Pauli padding law.\nFinally,\n`SequentialLocalFunctional.lean` descends these compatible values to the\ncorresponding `Module.DirectLimit` as a complex-linear functional.  It does\nnot construct multiplication or star on that quotient, positivity there, a\nnorm completion, or a quasilocal state.\n\n## I004 countable-representation status\n\n`CountablePauliRepresentation.lean` is the beginning of the subsequent\ncountable-lattice realization.  It defines the discrete countable binary\nconfiguration Hilbert space, count-measure translation operators, and bounded\none-site phase multipliers.  It proves their almost-everywhere action formulas,\ntranslation norm preservation, the zero-shift identity, translation\ncomposition, and the complete elementary `X`/`Z` generator relations:\ninvolution, same-family commutation, same-site anticommutation, and\ndistinct-site mixed commutation.  It also proves the additive initial/tail\n`Finsupp.filter` decomposition of configurations, including recomposition,\nthe two coordinate-vanishing properties, and the restrictions of a one-site\ngenerator to its appropriate side of a cut.  This is not yet an $L^2$\nfactorization.  The package does not yet prove a full phased Pauli\nrepresentation, the finite/tail matrix-algebra factorization, a concrete local\nstar-subalgebra chain, a norm-closed quasi-local algebra, or a global state.\nThe detailed resume record is\n`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/HANDOFF.md`.\nThe independent I004 reviews are at\n`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/reviews/`.\nThe final live FF05--FF07 closeout review is at\n`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF05-FF07-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\nFF08, project `5a41c5b2-24ef-4f49-9d6f-03e203a80ff3`, is accepted and\nintegrated.  Its quarantined archive contributes only the additive initial/tail\nsplit of `CountablePauliConfiguration`; the remote README attribution,\nstale HANDOFF deletion, and metadata were rejected.  The review is at\n`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF08-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\nFF09 is a remote-only candidate, project\n`f78a4014-b751-45d0-af0a-b1e8a9e32c11`: it asks only for the additive\nequivalence between the checked initial/tail configuration subgroups and has\nnot been retrieved or integrated.\n\nFF09 was subsequently set aside as off-track for the finite-fiber theorem:\nit remains remote-only and must not be retrieved or integrated merely because\nit completes an additive configuration decomposition.  FF10, project\n`88d5f994-e829-4ded-b04a-b38c650e4f8b`, has been accepted and integrated as\n`FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionQubitAlgebra.lean`.  Its archive SHA-256 is\n`7ca2f97893a1fc872626a0a7095b14887504c36939aa3b1e584cf086b0fa5778`; the\nremote snapshot remains quarantined under `aristotle_responses/FF10-extracted/`.\nOnly its candidate Lean file was used.  The returned local C-star instance was\npromoted to a named scoped instance so that the public norm theorem is usable\nby downstream files.  The module gives arbitrary finite-region qubit matrix\nalgebras and the one-inclusion `F \\subseteq F'` map `A \\mapsto A \\otimes 1`;\nit does not assert Pauli/stabilizer realization, triple-region coherence, a\ndirected colimit, quasilocal closure, state/GNS data, or the finite-fiber\ntheorem.  The task and its prompt review are under\n`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF10-finite-region-qubit-local-algebras.md`\nand `aristotle_responses/FF10-prompt-adversarial-review.md`; the post-result\nreview is `aristotle_responses/FF10-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n\nFF11, project `76d70d89-bf7a-490b-a1ee-6c3512437110`, was accepted and\nintegrated on August 5, 2026 as `FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionPauliMatrices.lean`.\nIts archive SHA-256 is\n`acaaeac3024447b211faf050224b9146e978d90c105da094a22b9226d84b529a` and the\ncomplete remote snapshot remains quarantined under\n`aristotle_responses/FF11-extracted/`.  Only\n`AristotleCandidates/FiniteRegionPauliMatrices.lean` was integrated; it is\nbyte-identical to the live source.  The remote README attribution insertion,\nstale deletion of the FF11 handoff status, `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md`, and its\nunverified claim of a commit/push were rejected.\n\nThe module realizes a phase-free Hermitian `PauliLabel` string as the\ncoordinate-free product of one-site matrix entries on every finite-region\nbasis.  It proves the all-identity and self-adjoint facts and that\n`finiteRegionEmbed` pads labels by `I`.  It deliberately does not represent or\nmultiply `FullPauliWord`: the `i^phase X^x Z^z` normal form still needs its\nfinite-region `ZMod 4`/Y-count phase aggregation.  No syntactic support/local-algebra\nidentification, triple-region coherence, colimit, state/GNS, or finite-fiber\nclaim is made.  Both independent reviews approve the surgical integration;\nthe task, prompt review, and post-result review are at\n`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF11-finite-region-pauli-matrices.md`,\n`aristotle_responses/FF11-prompt-adversarial-review.md`, and\n`aristotle_responses/FF11-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n\nFF12, project `c091ae7a-c696-4863-a46f-72c8ab6ca624`, was accepted and\nintegrated on August 5, 2026 as `FiniteFiber/OneSitePauliNormalForm.lean`.\nIts archive SHA-256 is\n`624b130a2c08061fa8f60edf33397c5a2dd82b4817569c0acdcd7f14c9da6cbf` and its\ncomplete remote snapshot remains quarantined under\n`aristotle_responses/FF12-extracted/`.  Only\n`AristotleCandidates/OneSitePauliNormalForm.lean` was integrated; it is\nbyte-identical to the live source with SHA-256\n`6d9e4ae4f3c0ae3a3c3b9d35322d42ddd8d518a07f75441b6b1a61a3984cfc99`.  The\nremote README attribution insertion, stale removal of the live FF12 status\nfrom the handoff, and `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md` were rejected.\n\nThe module proves the one-site conversion from the Hermitian representative\nto the raw normal form: `X Z = i^3 Y = -iY`.  Its phase correction is\nnonadditive and equals `3` only at the projective `Y` coordinate; it does not\nreuse `FullPauliWord.phaseEmbed`, which is the distinct sign map\n`1 ↦ 2`.  It does not define a finite-region or full-word representation,\nprove multiplication or cocycle compatibility, identify syntactic support\nwith local-algebra membership, or claim coherence, a colimit, state/GNS, or\nthe finite-fiber theorem.  Both independent post-result reviews approve the\nintegration.  The task, prompt review, and post-result review are at\n`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF12-one-site-pauli-normal-form.md`,\n`aristotle_responses/FF12-prompt-adversarial-review.md`, and\n`aristotle_responses/FF12-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n\nA later global stabilizer/GNS layer must still establish:\n\n\n--- INVESTIGATION HANDOFF ---\n# Handoff: I004 countable Pauli realization and quasi-local algebra\n\n## Resume point\n\nI004 has begun.  Its canonical scope and limits are in `QUESTION.tex` and\n`technical.tex`, both compiled successfully on August 3, 2026.  The new Lean\nfoundation is `formalization_finite_fibers/FiniteFiber/CountablePauliRepresentation.lean`.\n\nThe global finite-fiber theorem is **not** instantiated yet.  The current\nmodule only makes the first concrete countable representation ingredients\navailable.\n\n## What is checked now\n\nFor the countable finite-support binary configuration group\n\n```text\nK = ℕ →₀ ZMod 2,\nH = Lp ℂ 2 (Measure.count : Measure K),\n```\n\nthe package now has a discrete measurable-space instance and constructs:\n\n- `configurationBit i : K`, nonzero and of additive order two;\n- `configurationInitial n` and `configurationTail n`, the additive filters to\n  sites below and at-or-beyond the cut, respectively;\n- their recomposition theorem, their complementary coordinate-vanishing\n  theorems, and their action on a one-site configuration on the appropriate\n  side of the cut;\n- `configurationShift g : H →L[ℂ] H`, induced by count-measure-preserving\n  translation `x ↦ g + x`;\n- `configurationShift_zero`, proving that neutral translation is the identity;\n- `configurationShift_add`, proving\n  `configurationShift (g + h) = (configurationShift h).comp (configurationShift g)`;\n- `countablePauliX i`, the shift by `configurationBit i`;\n- `countablePauliX_comm`, proving that two such `X` translations commute;\n- `countablePauliX_comp_self`, proving that each one-site `X` generator is an\n  involution;\n- `phaseCharacter i : K → ℂ`, with square one and the correct same-site sign\n  flip / distinct-site invariance identities;\n- `configurationPhase i : H →L[ℂ] H`, obtained by bounded `L∞` multiplication;\n- `configurationPhase_comp_self`, proving that this phase operator squares to\n  the identity; and\n- `countablePauliZ i`, the corresponding local phase operator;\n- `countablePauliZ_comm`, proving that two `Z` generators commute;\n- `countablePauliZ_comp_countablePauliX_same`, proving same-site\n  anticommutation; and\n- `countablePauliZ_comp_countablePauliX_other`, proving mixed commutation at\n  distinct sites.\n\nThe checked action formulas are almost-everywhere formulas:\n\n```text\nconfigurationShift g f (x) = f (g + x),\nconfigurationPhase i f (x) = phaseCharacter i x * f x,\n```\n\nThe translation map preserves the `L²` norm exactly, has the checked\nzero-shift identity, and obeys the checked composition law above.  Thus the\nmodule now has the complete elementary `X`/`Z` generator relations, with all\nequalities of `Lp` representatives proved through their almost-everywhere\naction formulas.  At the configuration-group level it also has the checked\nadditive initial/tail split; this is a prerequisite for, but is not itself,\nthe finite/tail `L²` factorization.\n\n## What is deliberately not proved\n\nDo not promote this module to a countable Pauli matrix realization yet.  It\ndoes **not** currently prove:\n\n1. a full phased finite-support Pauli representation;\n2. the finite/tail Hilbert-space factorization and the identification of a\n   finite-site Pauli image with `M_(2^n)(ℂ) ⊗ 1`;\n3. a concrete increasing family of finite local star subalgebras;\n4. the norm-closed quasi-local C-star algebra;\n5. extension of compatible finite stabilizer functionals to a positive,\n   normalized state on that closure;\n6. the actual stabilizer-locality, GNS regional product-orbit, and\n   corner-traciality hypotheses needed to instantiate I002/I001.\n\nThus the manuscript theorem\n`thm:finite_projections_exist` remains only conditionally formalized through\nthe previously checked support-corner theorem.\n\n## Exact next Lean task\n\nFF01 promoted the shift-composition theorem on August 4, 2026.  The reviewed\ncandidate uses `MeasurePreserving.quasiMeasurePreserving.ae_eq_comp` to pull\nthe shift formula back along a translation and normalizes the composed map\nwith `ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply`; it is now permanent source, not a\ntemporary MWE.\n\nFF02 promoted the zero-shift identity, FF03 phase involution, and FF04 the\ncommutation of the `X` translations.  FF05--FF07 complete the remaining\nelementary bounded-operator relations, and FF08 completes the additive\ninitial/tail split of `CountablePauliConfiguration`.  FF09 was explicitly set\naside as irrelevant to the immediate finite-fiber proof route.\n\nThe direct finite-region bridge starts with accepted FF10\n(`FiniteRegionQubitAlgebra`), FF11 (`FiniteRegionPauliMatrices`), and now\nFF12 (`OneSitePauliNormalForm`).  FF12 fixes the one-site phase convention\nneeded to turn the Hermitian `Y` representative into the raw normal form\n`X Z = -iY`, with a `ZMod 4` correction of `3` at `Y`.  It neither builds a\nfinite-region/full-word map nor proves group multiplication.  The next bridge\nis a finite-region correction sum and padding formula, followed by the\nraw-cocycle/multiplication compatibility needed before any local-group\nrepresentation claim.  Any later countable operator construction must still\nkeep equality of `Lp` representatives almost-everywhere where applicable.\n\nFF02--FF04 were accepted and integrated on August 5, 2026: FF02\n(`f5883a1c-9605-4e52-aac0-c0ee8b5a928c`), FF03\n(`e18a3e80-c3c2-4f23-a320-ebfd9ac92cf9`), and FF04\n(`d9f4dcfc-d8a3-44a4-bc37-bb0aaf367c9e`).  Each returned snapshot is kept in\nits own `aristotle_responses/FF0*-extracted/` quarantine directory.  All three\nsnapshots contained the same unrelated README attribution insertion; it was\nrejected, and only the reviewed candidate Lean declarations were integrated.\nThe approved final reviews are\n`aristotle_responses/FF02-integration-adversarial-review.md`,\n`aristotle_responses/FF03-integration-adversarial-review.md`, and\n`aristotle_responses/FF04-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n\nFF05--FF07 were submitted in parallel and accepted on August 5, 2026: FF05 (one-site\n`X` involution), project `ea714466-c37d-41f0-8b86-7c4906330d56`; FF06\n(commutation of the `Z` phase generators), project\n`a8f2fb66-8bc7-41e3-be24-16aa5f57c192`; and FF07 (same-site mixed\nanticommutation and distinct-site mixed commutation), project\n`c280ca7f-3f19-40e9-9bd3-fd3a4e718cc5`.  Each returned snapshot is quarantined\nin its `aristotle_responses/FF0*-extracted/` directory.  As with FF02--FF04,\nevery snapshot contained an unrelated README attribution insertion; it was\nrejected, and only the reviewed candidate Lean declarations were integrated.\nTheir independent prompt audits are approved at\n`aristotle_responses/FF05-prompt-adversarial-review.md`,\n`aristotle_responses/FF06-prompt-adversarial-review.md`, and\n`aristotle_responses/FF07-prompt-adversarial-review.md`; the approved final\nintegration reviews are\n`aristotle_responses/FF05-integration-adversarial-review.md`,\n`aristotle_responses/FF06-integration-adversarial-review.md`, and\n`aristotle_responses/FF07-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n\nFF08, the additive initial/tail split of\n`CountablePauliConfiguration`, was accepted and integrated on August 5, 2026\nfrom project `5a41c5b2-24ef-4f49-9d6f-03e203a80ff3`.  Its archive\n`aristotle_responses/FF08-initial-tail-configuration-split.tar.gz` has SHA-256\n`a9355ae84e5a093aadfac197565a9376ad776f375028696f4bf0ebcf32716793` and is\nquarantined at `aristotle_responses/FF08-extracted/`.  Only\n`AristotleCandidates/InitialTailConfigurationSplit.lean` was integrated; the\nremote README attribution, stale HANDOFF deletion, and metadata were rejected.\nThe prompt audit and approved post-result review are\n`aristotle_responses/FF08-prompt-adversarial-review.md` and\n`aristotle_responses/FF08-integration-adversarial-review.md`.  Its scope is\nexactly the `Finsupp.filter` decomposition and its one-site consequences; it\ndoes not assert the needed Hilbert-space factorization or a local matrix\nalgebra.\n\nFF09, the additive equivalence between a configuration and its FF08\ninitial/tail components, was submitted to Aristotle on August 5, 2026 as\nproject `f78a4014-b751-45d0-af0a-b1e8a9e32c11`.  Its prompt audit is approved\nat `aristotle_responses/FF09-prompt-adversarial-review.md`.  It remains\nremote-only: no result has been retrieved or integrated.  It is constrained\nto an additive-subgroup equivalence of configurations and does not assert an\n`L²` factorization, finite-coordinate equivalence, matrix algebra, or GNS\nstatement.\n\n## Current bridge after FF09\n\nFF09 was explicitly set aside as irrelevant to the immediate finite-fiber\nproof route.  It remains remote-only and is not to be retrieved or integrated.\n\nFF10, project `88d5f994-e829-4ded-b04a-b38c650e4f8b`, was accepted and\nintegrated on August 5, 2026.  Its remote archive has SHA-256\n`7ca2f97893a1fc872626a0a7095b14887504c36939aa3b1e584cf086b0fa5778` and is\nquarantined at `aristotle_responses/FF10-extracted/`.  Only its candidate was\nintegrated as `formalization_finite_fibers/FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionQubitAlgebra.lean`.\nFor arbitrary `F \\subseteq F' : Finset Site`, it gives the finite-region\nqubit basis, the corresponding finite matrix algebra, a canonical basis split\ninto `F` and `F' \\ F`, and the reindexed `A \\mapsto A \\otimes 1` inclusion\nwith its explicit formula, injectivity, and operator-norm preservation.  The\ncandidate's file-local C-star instance was promoted to a named scoped instance\nso that downstream modules can use the norm theorem.  It makes no claim about\nPauli/stabilizer realization, compositional coherence, a local or quasilocal\ncolimit, state/GNS data, or the theorem on finite projections.  Its prompt and\npost-result reviews are `aristotle_responses/FF10-prompt-adversarial-review.md`\nand `aristotle_responses/FF10-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n\nFF11, project `76d70d89-bf7a-490b-a1ee-6c3512437110`, was accepted and\nintegrated on August 5, 2026.  Its archive\n`aristotle_responses/FF11-finite-region-pauli-matrices.tar.gz` has SHA-256\n`acaaeac3024447b211faf050224b9146e978d90c105da094a22b9226d84b529a`; the\ncomplete remote snapshot is quarantined at `aristotle_responses/FF11-extracted/`.\nOnly the returned candidate was integrated, byte-for-byte, as\n`formalization_finite_fibers/FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionPauliMatrices.lean`.\nThe remote README attribution insertion, stale FF11 handoff deletion,\n`ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md`, and unsupported commit/push claim were rejected.\n\nThe checked module realizes phase-free Hermitian Pauli-label strings directly\non arbitrary finite-region bases; it proves the all-identity and self-adjoint\nfacts and exact identity-padding compatibility with `finiteRegionEmbed`.  It\ndoes not represent or multiply `FullPauliWord`: the normal form\n`i^phase X^x Z^z` now has its one-site correction, but still requires\nfinite-region `ZMod 4`/Y-count aggregation.\nIt also makes no support/locality, coherence, colimit, state, GNS, or\nfinite-projection claim.  Both independent reviews approve the integration;\nsee `aristotle_responses/FF11-prompt-adversarial-review.md`,\n`aristotle_responses/FF11-integration-adversarial-review.md`, and\n`aristotle_tasks/FF11-finite-region-pauli-matrices.md`.\n\nFF12, project `c091ae7a-c696-4863-a46f-72c8ab6ca624`, was accepted and\nintegrated on August 5, 2026.  Its archive\n`aristotle_responses/FF12-one-site-pauli-normal-form.tar.gz` has SHA-256\n`624b130a2c08061fa8f60edf33397c5a2dd82b4817569c0acdcd7f14c9da6cbf`; the\ncomplete remote snapshot is quarantined at `aristotle_responses/FF12-extracted/`.\nOnly `AristotleCandidates/OneSitePauliNormalForm.lean` was integrated,\nbyte-for-byte, as `formalization_finite_fibers/FiniteFiber/OneSitePauliNormalForm.lean`\n(source SHA-256\n`6d9e4ae4f3c0ae3a3c3b9d35322d42ddd8d518a07f75441b6b1a61a3984cfc99`).  The\nremote README attribution insertion, stale FF12 handoff deletion, and\n`ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md` were rejected.\n\nThe checked module proves exactly `X Z = i^3Y = -iY` and the corresponding\nnonadditive correction `3` at the projective `Y` coordinate.  It does not\nreuse the sign map `phaseEmbed 1 = 2`, nor does it make a finite-region,\nfull-word, cocycle, local-group, quasilocal, GNS, or finite-projection claim.\nIts prompt and post-result reviews are\n`aristotle_responses/FF12-prompt-adversarial-review.md` and\n`aristotle_responses/FF12-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n\n## Verification record\n\nPassed after integrating FF01--FF08:\n\n```bash\ncd formalization_finite_fibers\nlake env lean FiniteFiber/CountablePauliRepresentation.lean\nlake build FiniteFiber.CountablePauliRepresentation\nlake build FiniteFiber\nlake build\nlake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean\n```\n\nThe public-theorem audit now includes `configurationShift_zero`,\n`countablePauliX_comm`, `configurationPhase_comp_self`,\n`countablePauliX_comp_self`, `countablePauliZ_comm`,\n`countablePauliZ_comp_countablePauliX_same`, and\n`countablePauliZ_comp_countablePauliX_other`,\n`configurationInitial_add_configurationTail`,\n`configurationInitial_apply_of_le`, `configurationTail_apply_of_lt`,\n`configurationInitial_bit_of_lt`, and `configurationTail_bit_of_le`.  Their\nexpected axioms remain only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`;\nno project-local axiom, `sorry`, `admit`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, or\n`implemented_by` declaration is present in the new module.\n\nFF11 was verified after integration with:\n\n```bash\ncd formalization_finite_fibers\nlake env lean FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionPauliMatrices.lean\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionPauliMatrices\nlake build FiniteFiber\nlake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean\nlake build\n\n--- MEMORY MATCHES ---\n88-### keywords\n89-\n90:- thm:finite_projections_exist, full_tracial_corner_semifinite, finite fibers, central projection, qMq, fullness, formalization_finite_fibers, VNTrace\n91-\n92-## Task 2: build and review the countable configuration-space L² Pauli foundation\n--\n109-\n110-- The live theorem is `writing/overleaf_prl_stabilizer_region_algebras/main.tex:1501` (`thm:finite_projections_exist`): every nonzero central projection `z` has a finite nonzero projection in `zM_Γ`. The stronger reusable target is `full_tracial_corner_semifinite`: a faithful tracial corner `qMq` plus full `q` implies each nonzero central summand contains a finite nonzero projection; finite central fibers/sectors are a corollary, not finite-dimensional fibers. [Task 1]\n111:- Use the standalone `formalization_finite_fibers/` package, preserving `work/OLD/formalization/`. Its old `VNTrace` interface is too weak for complex-linear trace subtraction such as `τ(q - vv*) = 0`. [Task 1]\n112-- `FiniteFiber/CountablePauliRepresentation.lean` realizes `K := ℕ →₀ ZMod 2` and `H := Lp ℂ 2 (Measure.count)`, with translations and bounded phase multipliers. Lp action formulas are almost-everywhere (`=ᵐ[Measure.count]`): translations use `MeasureTheory.measurePreserving_add_left` and `MeasureTheory.Lp.compMeasurePreservingₗᵢ`; phase multiplication uses an L∞ certificate and `ContinuousLinearMap.holderL`. [Task 2]\n113-- Verify with focused and full `lake build`, `lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean`, direct theorem audits, and the handoff. Checked declarations used only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`; both independent reviews were APPROVED. [Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
