{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- ARISTOTLE REFERENCE ---' && sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- I004 HANDOFF FF13+ ---' && rg -n -C 3 'FF1[3-7]|FullPauliStabilizerDensity|next prepared|status' history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/HANDOFF.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- RESPONSE AREA ---' && find history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%p\\\\n' | sort | tail -80 && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- TASK LOG ---' && tail -80 history/logs/20260806T191928Z-a8623a7e-tasks.log && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- LIVE CANDIDATE STATUS ---' && find FiniteFiber -maxdepth 1 -type f -name '*FullPauli*' -printf '%f\\\\n' && printf '%s\\\\n' '--- MANUSCRIPT ---' && rg --files .. -g 'main.tex' | rg 'manuscript|I004|writing' | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"--- ARISTOTLE REFERENCE ---\n# Aristotle CLI reference\n\n## Setup\n\n- Install: `uv tool install aristotlelib`\n- Verify: `aristotle --version`\n- Authenticate: set `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` in the shell environment, or use the skill wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\nIf the key is stored near the end of `~/.bashrc`, noninteractive commands may not see it because many `.bashrc` files contain:\n\n```bash\ncase $- in\n    *i*) ;;\n      *) return;;\nesac\n```\n\nIn that case, do not rely on `source ~/.bashrc`. Use the wrapper, which reads a literal `export ARISTOTLE_API_KEY=...` assignment without printing it:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize input.md\n```\n\n## Core commands\n\nSubmit a Lean project for sorry filling or proof search:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh submit \"Fill in all sorries\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\nFormalize a TeX or paper source:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize paper.tex --wait --destination output.tar.gz\n```\n\nList recent jobs:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh list --limit 10\n```\n\nDownload a completed job:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh download <project-id> --destination result.tar.gz\n```\n\nPass the key directly for one command only:\n\n```bash\naristotle submit \"My prompt\" --api-key \"$ARISTOTLE_API_KEY\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\n## Recommended project loop\n\n1. Inspect the Lean project locally.\n2. Run the narrowest local build or test that exercises the target files.\n3. Submit a focused Aristotle prompt against the project directory.\n4. Wait for the run if the expected result is a concrete patch.\n5. Download or inspect the produced artifact.\n6. Rebuild locally and repeat with a tighter prompt if needed.\n\n## Prompt shape\n\nKeep prompts short and file-bound. Good prompts mention:\n\n- the exact project directory\n- the theorem or file to work on\n- whether to fill `sorry`s, formalize a statement, or debug a failing proof\n- what counts as a useful partial result\n\nAvoid vague prompts such as \"improve this project\" unless the scope is intentionally broad.\n--- I004 HANDOFF FF13+ ---\n306-  insertion.\n307-- `aristotle_responses/FF05-FF07-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`\n308-  independently rechecks the live integration, AE/Lp representative handling,\n309:  theorem scope, permanent status records, and attribution quarantine.\n310-- `aristotle_responses/FF08-integration-adversarial-review.md` approves the\n311-  additive initial/tail candidate only and rejects the remote README\n312-  attribution, stale HANDOFF deletion, and metadata.\n313-\n314:## FF13--FF14 closeout\n315-\n316:FF13 and FF14 are integrated into `formalization_finite_fibers` after fresh\n317-adversarial review. The next bounded package is finite-region realization of\n318-`FullPauliWord` multiplication and its cocycle/central-phase compatibility.\n319-The quasilocal algebra, global state, GNS representation, and infinite\n--\n339-- I004 and `formalization_finite_fibers/` are currently untracked package/work\n340-  artifacts; no commit or push was made.\n341-\n342:## FF15 closeout: finite-region full-Pauli multiplication\n343-\n344-**Proved.**  `FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication.lean` is\n345-integrated after quarantine review of Aristotle task\n--\n366-colimit or norm closure, produce a state or GNS representation, or advance\n367-the infinite finite-projection theorem.\n368-\n369:**Blocked / failed.**  None within FF15's stated finite-region scope.  The\n370-remote snapshot's unrelated files and metadata were not integrated.\n371-\n372-The raw archive is quarantined at\n373:`aristotle_responses/FF15-finite-region-full-pauli-multiplication.tar.gz`;\n374-the reviewed candidate module is byte-identical to the live module.  The\n375-live verification and adversarial record is\n376:`aristotle_responses/FF15-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\n377-\n378-\n379:## FF16 closeout: full-Pauli support and finite-region locality\n380-\n381-**Proved.** `FiniteFiber/FullPauliSupportLocality.lean` is integrated after quarantine review of Aristotle task `a1684489-8deb-4f62-8f5a-a592570dd778`. For `a : FullPauliWord Site`, it defines `a.SupportedIn F := a.label.support ⊆ F` and a finite-only realization predicate requiring one `A : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F` to identity-pad to `fullPauliRegionMatrix F' a` for every finite `F ⊆ F'`. It proves\n382-\n--\n396-\n397-**Partial.** This is finite support/local-matrix infrastructure only. It does not identify syntactic support with local-algebra membership, construct a global/quasilocal algebra, state or GNS data, or advance the finite-projection theorem.\n398-\n399:**Blocked / failed.** None within FF16 scope. The remote umbrella import, README/metadata, manuscript copy, and every other noncandidate snapshot file were rejected. The raw archive is `aristotle_responses/FF16-full-pauli-support-locality.tar.gz` (SHA-256 `447389053d147319b70c0c519f027c25bfc78c085dcfca68c23e4b793345b727`); the complete snapshot remains at `aristotle_responses/FF16-extracted/`. The integration review is `aristotle_responses/FF16-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\n400-\n401:Live checks passed: `lake build FiniteFiber.FullPauliSupportLocality`, `lake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication`, `lake build FiniteFiber`, `lake build`, `lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean`, and a direct `#print axioms` audit for every FF16 public theorem. Each FF16 theorem uses only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n--- RESPONSE AREA ---\nhistory/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF01-adversarial-review.md\nhistory/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF01-countable-shift-composition.tar.gz\nhistory/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF01-integration-adversarial-review.md\nhistory/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF02-FF04-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md\nhistory/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF02-countable-shift-zero.tar.gz\nhistory/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF02-integration-adversarial-review.md\nhistory/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF02-prompt-adversarial-review.md\nhistory/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF03-countable-phase-involution.tar.gz\nhistory/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF03-integration-adversarial-review.md\nhistory/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aris