n179-\n180-If on a Hilbert space with $N$ qubits and one has $N$ stabilizers, the codespace is uniquely fixed to a single state, a so-called stabilizer state. \n181:For this state, the reduced density matrix for any subsystem\n182-is fixed to the form \n183-\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:projection_state}\n184:  \\rho_{\\Gamma}=\\frac{P_{\\cS}}{\\operatorname{rank}P_{\\cS}},\n185-\\end{equation}\n186-where $P_{\\cS}$ is a projection \\cite{Fattal:2004frh}.\n187:The density matrix of such stabilizer states\n188-therefore has a flat spectrum.\n189-More generally all states that arise from acting with Clifford circuits, circuits that only contain Pauli operators, Hadamard, CNOT or phase gates, on a product state in the computational basis are stabilizer\n190-states. This is an important characteristic of these states, since by the Gottesman--Knill theorem, it is exactly\n--\n254-the Unruh effect \\cite{Unruh:1976db}, which establishes that the vacuum of\n255-Minkowski spacetime appears like a thermal state for an observer that\n256-experience a constant acceleration, a so-called Rindler observer.\n257:This suggests that the reduced density matrix of the vacuum is\n258-\\begin{equation}\n259-    \\r_R = \\frac{e^{-2 \\pi K_R}}{Z},\n260-\\end{equation}\n--\n264-\\end{equation}\n265-is the restriction of the boost generator to the region causally accessible to\n266-this observer. All these expressions have to be taken with care, since due to\n267:the type III$_1$ nature of the local algebras, the reduced density matrix is\n268-not rigorously defined. The algebraic incarnation of the Unruh effect is the Bisognano-Wichmann\n269-theorem \\cite{Bisognano:1976za}, which states that the modular operator for the local algebra $\\cA_W$, associated to a Wedge $W$\n270-is given by\n--\n280-\\end{equation}\n281-where the intersection is over all \\textit{faithful normal} states of $\\cA$,\n282-i.e. the spectrum of all modular operators is continuous, which in turn implies\n283:that all reduced density matrices should have non-flat spectra.\n284-All these considerations suggest that our fundamental idea is\n285-consistent with relativistic invariance.\\\\\n286-\n--\n348-We now discuss our theory for the simpler case of a version of short-range range ordered\n349-states. As discussed more deeply in Appendix \\ref{app:short_range}, we say that a stabilizer system has short-range order in the region $\\G$, if the associated state\n350-is made up of products of states living in finitely sized regions.\n351:In Appendix \\LS{REF}, we then show that the reduced density matrix of the state can be\n352-put into the form\n353-\\begin{equation}\n354:    \\rho_{\\Gamma_n} \\sim \n355- \\ket{\\mathbf 0_n}\\!\\bra{\\mathbf 0_n}\n356- \\otimes\\frac{\\id_{\\cC_n}}{\\dim\\cC_n}\n357- \\otimes\\frac{\\id_{\\cX_n}}{\\dim\\cX_n}.\n--\n396-\n397-For a finite interval $\\Gamma$, the canonical local state is proportional to\n398-\\begin{equation}\n399:    \\rho_\\Gamma=\\ket{\\mathbf0}\\!\\bra{\\mathbf0} +\\ket{\\mathbf1}\\!\\bra{\\mathbf1}.\n400-\\end{equation}\n401-The two terms label the all-zero and all-one sectors and for the half-chain\n402-indexed by positive labels $n>0$, the local algebra $\\cM_>$ becomes\n--\n787-$\\cA$. The representations $\\pi_1$ and $\\pi_2$ are called quasi-equivalent if\n788-and only if there exists a $\\sigma$-weakly bicontinuous $\\ast$-isomorphism\n789-\\begin{equation}\n790:    \\rho:M_{\\pi_1} \\rightarrow M_{\\pi_2}\n791-\\end{equation}\n792-such that\n793-\\begin{equation}\n794:    \\rho(\\pi_1(a)) = \\pi_2(a),\n795-    \\quad a\\in\\cA.\n796-\\end{equation}\n797-\\end{definition}\n--\n880-\n881-The \\textit{stabilizer group} $\\cG_{\\cS}$ is the group generated by finite\n882-products of elements of $\\cS$. For a finite region $F\\Subset\\cL$, the\n883:\\textit{local stabilizer group} is\n884-\\begin{equation}\n885-    \\cG_{\\cS,F}=\\cG_{\\cS}\\cap\\cA_F.\n886-\\end{equation}\n--\n896-    \\qquad g\\in\\cG_{\\cS,F},\n897-\\end{equation}\n898-and therefore projects onto the common $+1$ eigenspace of all stabilizers.\n899:This defines a local density matrix\n900-\\begin{equation}\n901:    \\rho_F=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_F)}P_F.\n902-\\end{equation}\n903-We can compute\n904-\\begin{equation}\n--\n909-operators are traceless. Therefore, only the identity contributes, which gives the factor\n910-$2^{|F|}$. We therefore find that\n911-\\begin{equation}\n912:    \\rho_F=\\frac{1}{2^{|F|}}\\sum_{g\\in\\cG_{\\cS,F}}g.\n913:    \\label{eq:local_density_full}\n914-\\end{equation}\n915-\n916-We now note that if $F\\subset F'$ are finite subsets of $\\cL$, we have\n917:\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:rho-compatibility}\n918:    \\rho_F=\\operatorname{Tr}_{F'\\setminus F}(\\rho_{F'}).\n919-\\end{equation}\n920-This can be seen by the fact that\n921-\\begin{equation}\n--\n932-\\end{equation}\n933-Which in turn implies\n934-\\begin{align}\n935:    \\operatorname{Tr}_{F'\\setminus F}(\\rho_{F'})\n936-    &=\\frac{1}{2^{|F'|}}\n937-      \\sum_{g\\in\\cG_{\\cS,F'}}\n938-      \\operatorname{Tr}_{F'\\setminus F}(g) \\\\\n939-    &=\\frac{1}{2^{|F'|}}2^{|F'\\setminus F|}\n940-      \\sum_{g\\in\\cG_{\\cS,F}}g \\\\\n941-    &=\\frac{1}{2^{|F|}}\\sum_{g\\in\\cG_{\\cS,F}}g\n942:      =\\rho_F.\n943-\\end{align}\n944-Here we used that for $g\\in\\cG_{\\cS,F}$,\n945-\\begin{equation}\n--\n952-quasi-local algebra via\n953-\\begin{proposition}\\label{prop:define_state}\n954-    Let $\\cS$ be a consistent stabilizer system on a lattice $\\cL$. Then the\n955:    state defined by the reduced density matrices $\\rho_F$ above defines a\n956-    unique state on $\\cA$.\n957-\\end{proposition}\n958-\\begin{proof}\n959:    The local density matrices already define the state\n960-    \\begin{equation}\n961:        \\w(a):=\\operatorname{Tr}_F(\\rho_Fa),\n962-        \\qquad a\\in\\cA_F.\n963-    \\end{equation}\n964-    The consistency relation\n965-    \\begin{equation}\n966:        \\rho_F=\\operatorname{Tr}_{F'\\setminus F}(\\rho_{F'})\n967-    \\end{equation}\n968-    proves that the state is independent of the representation. So that if\n969-    $a$ is considered as an element of $\\cA_F$ and of $\\cA_{F'}$, then\n970-    \\begin{align}\n971:        \\operatorname{Tr}_{F'}\\bigl(\\rho_{F'}(a\\otimes\\id_{F'\\setminus F})\\bigr)\n972:        &=\\operatorname{Tr}_F\\bigl(\\operatorname{Tr}_{F'\\setminus F}(\\rho_{F'})a\\bigr) \\\\\n973:        &=\\operatorname{Tr}_F(\\rho_Fa).\n974-    \\end{align}\n975-    Therefore, the state is well-defined on elements in $\\cA_{\\text{loc}}$.\n976-    Since by definition $\\cA_{\\text{loc}}$ is a norm-dense subset of $\\cA$,\n--\n993-    Furthermore,\n994-    \\begin{equation}\n995-        \\w(c_n^*c_n)\n996:        =\\operatorname{Tr}_{F_n}(\\rho_{F_n}c_n^*c_n)\\geq0,\n997-    \\end{equation}\n998-    which implies $\\w(a)\\geq0$. \n999-\\end{proof}\n--\n1057-\n1058-\\begin{lemma}\n1059-    Let $\\cH_{12} = \\cH_1 \\otimes \\cH_2$ be a tensor product of finite dimensional\n1060:    Hilbert spaces, $\\r_{12}$ a density matrix of $\\cH_{12}$ with marginal\n1061-    $\\r_1 = \\Tr_{2} \\r_{12}$ and for any hermitean operator let \n1062-    $s(\\r)$ be the projection onto the eigenspace of $\\r$, i.e. if \n1063-    \\begin{equation}\n--\n1100-\\end{proof}\n1101-\n1102-\\begin{proof}[Proof of Lemma \\ref{lema:proj_inequality}]\n1103:    Since by Eq. \\eqref{eq:rho-compatibility} $\\r_{\\G_n} = \\Tr_{\\G_{n+1} \\setminus \\G_{n}} \\r_{\\G_{n+1}}$, the previous lemma implies\n1104-    \\begin{equation}\n1105-        s(\\r_{\\G_n}) \\otimes \\id_{\\G_{n+1} \\setminus \\G_{n}} \\geq s(\\r_{\\G_{n+1}}).\n1106-    \\end{equation}\n--\n1272-Neumann algebra considered on the Hilbert space $q \\cH_\\w$.\n1273-To proof the assertion, we need to first proof, that $q \\cU_\\G q$ is strongly\n1274-dense in $q M_\\G q$, to approximate the functional on it.\n1275:For that, let $x \\in M_\\G$. By Kaplanskys Density theorem\n1276-\\cite[I.9.1.3]{Blackadar}, there exist a uniformly bounded net $(x_i)_{i\\in I}$ in $\\cU_\\G$ with $x_i \\xrightarrow{\\sigma\\text{-}\\mathrm{s}} x$ and hence\n1277-strongly. By the same argument as in the previous lemma then\n--- SCOPE CLAIM SCAN ---\n70:No countable stabilizer system is inferred from short-range order, no\n71:exhaustion, no quasilocal algebra, no state on an infinite system, and no GNS\n674:finite region.  No countability, exhaustion, or long-range-order input is\n--- CANDIDATE VS QUARANTINE ---\n688162cc2779855e163f45fd210e4ddd36339579136fd3039f19df82cfca0a09  FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean\n688162cc2779855e163f45fd210e4ddd36339579136fd3039f19df82cfca0a09  history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF17-extracted/aristotle-finite_fiber-dn856r4c_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean\n--- NEW MODULE DIFF STAT ---\n .../FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean                | 820 +++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 820 insertions(+)\n--- CURRENT TARGET STATUS ---\n?? FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean\n?? ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean | sed -n '300,545p;645,720p' && nl -ba <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '106,115p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean | sed -n '300,545p;645,720p' && nl -ba <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '106,115p'\"","aggregated_output":"   300\tits elements.  Every hypothesis of the finite-density identity below is a\n   301\tfield of this structure; nothing is inferred from an infinite lattice.\n   302\t-/\n   303\tstructure FullPauliRegionStabilizer (Site : Type*) [DecidableEq Site] where\n   304\t  /-- The stabilizer subgroup of the algebraic full-Pauli group. -/\n   305\t  group : Subgroup (FullPauliWord Site)\n   306\t  /-- The finite region carrying the matrix realization. -/\n   307\t  region : Finset Site\n   308\t  /-- The explicit finiteness datum of the subgroup. -/\n   309\t  groupFintype : Fintype ↥group\n   310\t  /-- Every stabilizer is syntactically supported in the region. -/\n   311\t  supported : ∀ g ∈ group, (g : FullPauliWord Site).label.support ⊆ region\n   312\t  /-- Every stabilizer squares to the identity word (algebraic Hermiticity). -/\n   313\t  involutive : ∀ g ∈ group, g * g = 1\n   314\t  /-- Consistency: the central word `-1` is not a stabilizer. -/\n   315\t  consistent : FullPauliWord.negativeIdentity (Site := Site) ∉ group\n   316\t\n   317\tattribute [instance] FullPauliRegionStabilizer.groupFintype\n   318\t\n   319\tnamespace FullPauliRegionStabilizer\n   320\t\n   321\tvariable (D : FullPauliRegionStabilizer Site)\n   322\t\n   323\t/-- A finite involutive subgroup is abelian, hence a consistent stabilizer group. -/\n   324\tnoncomputable def toConsistentStabilizerGroup : FullPauliWord.ConsistentStabilizerGroup Site where\n   325\t  group := D.group\n   326\t  commute := by\n   327\t    intro g h\n   328\t    have hgh : ((g : FullPauliWord Site) * h) * ((g : FullPauliWord Site) * h) = 1 :=\n   329\t      D.involutive _ (mul_mem g.2 h.2)\n   330\t    have hg : (g : FullPauliWord Site) = (g : FullPauliWord Site)⁻¹ :=\n   331\t      eq_inv_of_mul_eq_one_left (D.involutive _ g.2)\n   332\t    have hh : (h : FullPauliWord Site) = (h : FullPauliWord Site)⁻¹ :=\n   333\t      eq_inv_of_mul_eq_one_left (D.involutive _ h.2)\n   334\t    show (g : FullPauliWord Site) * h = (h : FullPauliWord Site) * g\n   335\t    calc (g : FullPauliWord Site) * h = ((g : FullPauliWord Site) * h)⁻¹ :=\n   336\t          eq_inv_of_mul_eq_one_left hgh\n   337\t      _ = (h : FullPauliWord Site)⁻¹ * (g : FullPauliWord Site)⁻¹ := mul_inv_rev _ _\n   338\t      _ = (h : FullPauliWord Site) * g := by rw [← hg, ← hh]\n   339\t  involutive := fun g => D.involutive _ g.2\n   340\t  no_negative_identity := D.consistent\n   341\t\n   342\t/-- A stabilizer with trivial projective label is the identity word. -/\n   343\ttheorem eq_one_of_label_eq_zero (g : D.group)\n   344\t    (hlabel : (g : FullPauliWord Site).label = 0) :\n   345\t    (g : FullPauliWord Site) = 1 :=\n   346\t  FullPauliWord.element_eq_one_of_label_eq_zero D.toConsistentStabilizerGroup g hlabel\n   347\t\n   348\t/--\n   349\tA stabilizer whose finite-region matrix is a nonzero scalar multiple of the\n   350\tidentity is the identity word.  This is the consistency step: tracelessness of\n   351\tnonidentity Pauli strings forces the trivial label, and the excluded central\n   352\tword `-1` then forces the trivial phase.\n   353\t-/\n   354\ttheorem eq_one_of_regionMatrix_eq_smul_one (g : D.group) (c : ℂ) (hc : c ≠ 0)\n   355\t    (h : fullPauliRegionMatrix D.region (g : FullPauliWord Site) = c • 1) :\n   356\t    (g : FullPauliWord Site) = 1 := by\n   357\t  refine D.eq_one_of_label_eq_zero g ?_\n   358\t  by_contra hne\n   359\t  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Finsupp.ne_iff.mp hne\n   360\t  simp only [Finsupp.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply] at hi\n   361\t  have hiF : i ∈ D.region :=\n   362\t    D.supported _ g.2 (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr hi)\n   363\t  have hlabelI : regionPauliLabels D.region (g : FullPauliWord Site) ⟨i, hiF⟩ ≠\n   364\t      PauliLabel.I := by\n   365\t    rw [regionPauliLabels, FullPauliWord.localPauliLabel,\n   366\t      Ne, PauliLabel.ofProjectiveCoordinates_eq_I_iff]\n   367\t    exact hi\n   368\t  have htr0 : (fullPauliRegionMatrix D.region (g : FullPauliWord Site)).trace = 0 := by\n   369\t    rw [fullPauliRegionMatrix_eq_regionHermitianPhase_smul, Matrix.trace_smul,\n   370\t      trace_finiteRegionPauliMatrix_eq_zero_of_exists_ne_I _ _ ⟨⟨i, hiF⟩, hlabelI⟩,\n   371\t      smul_zero]\n   372\t  rw [h, Matrix.trace_smul, Matrix.trace_one, card_finiteRegionBasis] at htr0\n   373\t  exact hc (by simpa [pow_ne_zero] using htr0)\n   374\t\n   375\t/-- The finite-region matrix realization of the stabilizer subgroup. -/\n   376\tnoncomputable def regionRepresentation :\n   377\t    D.group →* Matrix (QubitIndex D.region.card) (QubitIndex D.region.card) ℂ where\n   378\t  toFun g := regionToQubitMatrix D.region\n   379\t    (fullPauliRegionMatrix D.region (g : FullPauliWord Site))\n   380\t  map_one' := by\n   381\t    rw [show ((1 : D.group) : FullPauliWord Site) = 1 from rfl,\n   382\t      fullPauliRegionMatrix_one, map_one]\n   383\t  map_mul' g h := by\n   384\t    rw [show ((g * h : D.group) : FullPauliWord Site) =\n   385\t        (g : FullPauliWord Site) * h from rfl,\n   386\t      fullPauliRegionMatrix_mul _ _ _ (D.supported _ g.2), map_mul]\n   387\t\n   388\t@[simp] theorem regionRepresentation_apply (g : D.group) :\n   389\t    D.regionRepresentation g =\n   390\t      regionToQubitMatrix D.region\n   391\t        (fullPauliRegionMatrix D.region (g : FullPauliWord Site)) := rfl\n   392\t\n   393\t/-- The realization is injective on the stabilizer subgroup. -/\n   394\ttheorem regionRepresentation_injective : Function.Injective D.regionRepresentation := by\n   395\t  rw [injective_iff_map_eq_one]\n   396\t  intro g hg\n   397\t  apply Subtype.ext\n   398\t  refine D.eq_one_of_regionMatrix_eq_smul_one g 1 one_ne_zero ?_\n   399\t  rw [one_smul]\n   400\t  apply (regionToQubitMatrix D.region).injective\n   401\t  rw [map_one]\n   402\t  exact hg\n   403\t\n   404\t/-- No stabilizer is realized by the central matrix `-1`. -/\n   405\ttheorem regionRepresentation_ne_neg_one (g : D.group) :\n   406\t    D.regionRepresentation g ≠\n   407\t      (-1 : Matrix (QubitIndex D.region.card) (QubitIndex D.region.card) ℂ) := by\n   408\t  intro hneg\n   409\t  have hmatrix : fullPauliRegionMatrix D.region (g : FullPauliWord Site) =\n   410\t      (-1 : ℂ) • 1 := by\n   411\t    apply (regionToQubitMatrix D.region).injective\n   412\t    rw [map_smul, map_one]\n   413\t    simpa using hneg\n   414\t  have hone : (g : FullPauliWord Site) = 1 :=\n   415\t    D.eq_one_of_regionMatrix_eq_smul_one g (-1) (by norm_num) hmatrix\n   416\t  rw [hone, fullPauliRegionMatrix_one] at hmatrix\n   417\t  have hentry := congrFun (congrFun hmatrix (fun _ => 0)) (fun _ => 0)\n   418\t  rw [Matrix.one_apply_eq, Matrix.smul_apply, Matrix.one_apply_eq] at hentry\n   419\t  norm_num at hentry\n   420\t\n   421\t/--\n   422\t**The abstract finite-density data.**  The finite consistent stabilizer\n   423\tsubgroup, its finite-region matrix image and the Hermitian sign convention\n   424\t`regionSign` assemble into the signed-Pauli stabilizer data of the\n   425\tfinite-density layer.  Faithfulness and the exclusion of `-1` are proved, not\n   426\tassumed.\n   427\t-/\n   428\tnoncomputable def stabilizerData :\n   429\t    FinitePauliStabilizerData D.group D.region.card where\n   430\t  representation := D.regionRepresentation\n   431\t  negative g := regionSign D.region (g : FullPauliWord Site)\n   432\t  labels g j :=\n   433\t    regionPauliLabels D.region (g : FullPauliWord Site) (D.region.equivFin.symm j)\n   434\t  representation_eq g := by\n   435\t    rw [regionRepresentation_apply,\n   436\t      fullPauliRegionMatrix_eq_pauliSign_smul _ _ (D.supported _ g.2)\n   437\t        (D.involutive _ g.2),\n   438\t      map_smul, regionToQubitMatrix_pauliMatrix]\n   439\t    exact (FinitePauliStabilizerData.signedPauliStringMatrix_eq_signedPauliTerm _ _).symm\n   440\t  injective := D.regionRepresentation_injective\n   441\t  no_negative_identity := D.regionRepresentation_ne_neg_one\n   442\t\n   443\t/-! ### The finite-region stabilizer density -/\n   444\t\n   445\t/-- The unnormalized local stabilizer sum `∑_{g ∈ G} g` on the region. -/\n   446\tnoncomputable def regionSum : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra D.region :=\n   447\t  ∑ g : D.group, fullPauliRegionMatrix D.region (g : FullPauliWord Site)\n   448\t\n   449\t/-- The local code projector `P_F = |G|⁻¹ ∑_{g ∈ G} g` of the manuscript. -/\n   450\tnoncomputable def regionProjector : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra D.region :=\n   451\t  (Fintype.card D.group : ℂ)⁻¹ • D.regionSum\n   452\t\n   453\t/-- The local density matrix `ρ_F = 2^{-|F|} ∑_{g ∈ G} g` of the manuscript. -/\n   454\tnoncomputable def regionDensity : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra D.region :=\n   455\t  ((2 : ℂ) ^ D.region.card)⁻¹ • D.regionSum\n   456\t\n   457\t/-- The basis identification carries the local sum to the abstract sum. -/\n   458\ttheorem regionToQubitMatrix_regionSum :\n   459\t    regionToQubitMatrix D.region D.regionSum = D.stabilizerData.stabilizerSum := by\n   460\t  rw [regionSum, map_sum]\n   461\t  rfl\n   462\t\n   463\t/-- The basis identification carries the local code projector to the abstract one. -/\n   464\ttheorem regionToQubitMatrix_regionProjector :\n   465\t    regionToQubitMatrix D.region D.regionProjector =\n   466\t      D.stabilizerData.stabilizerProjector := by\n   467\t  rw [regionProjector, map_smul, regionToQubitMatrix_regionSum]\n   468\t  rfl\n   469\t\n   470\t/--\n   471\t**The finite density identity.**  After the canonical basis identification of\n   472\tthe finite region with the `|F|`-qubit computational basis, the group average\n   473\t`ρ_F = 2^{-|F|} ∑_{g ∈ G} g` of the finite-region matrix image is *exactly* the\n   474\tstabilizer density constructed abstractly in the finite-density layer, with the\n   475\tsame sign and central-phase convention.\n   476\t-/\n   477\ttheorem regionToQubitMatrix_regionDensity :\n   478\t    regionToQubitMatrix D.region D.regionDensity =\n   479\t      D.stabilizerData.stabilizerDensity := by\n   480\t  rw [regionDensity, map_smul, regionToQubitMatrix_regionSum]\n   481\t  rfl\n   482\t\n   483\t/-- The basis identification preserves adjoints. -/\n   484\ttheorem regionToQubitMatrix_star (F : Finset Site) (A : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F) :\n   485\t    regionToQubitMatrix F (star A) = star (regionToQubitMatrix F A) := rfl\n   486\t\n   487\t/-! ### The manuscript's finite-volume conclusions -/\n   488\t\n   489\t/-- Every stabilizer fixes the local code projector: `g P_F = P_F`. -/\n   490\ttheorem fullPauliRegionMatrix_mul_regionProjector (g : D.group) :\n   491\t    fullPauliRegionMatrix D.region (g : FullPauliWord Site) * D.regionProjector =\n   492\t      D.regionProjector := by\n   493\t  apply (regionToQubitMatrix D.region).injective\n   494\t  rw [map_mul, regionToQubitMatrix_regionProjector]\n   495\t  exact D.stabilizerData.representation_mul_stabilizerProjector_left g\n   496\t\n   497\t/-- The local code projector is a self-adjoint idempotent. -/\n   498\ttheorem regionProjector_isStarProjection : IsStarProjection D.regionProjector := by\n   499\t  constructor\n   500\t  · apply (regionToQubitMatrix D.region).injective\n   501\t    rw [map_mul, regionToQubitMatrix_regionProjector]\n   502\t    exact D.stabilizerData.stabilizerProjector_isIdempotent\n   503\t  · change star D.regionProjector = D.regionProjector\n   504\t    apply (regionToQubitMatrix D.region).injective\n   505\t    rw [regionToQubitMatrix_star, regionToQubitMatrix_regionProjector]\n   506\t    exact D.stabilizerData.stabilizerProjector_isSelfAdjoint\n   507\t\n   508\t/-- The local code projector has the manuscript's trace `2^{|F|}/|G|`. -/\n   509\ttheorem regionProjector_trace :\n   510\t    D.regionProjector.trace = (Fintype.card D.group : ℂ)⁻¹ * (2 : ℂ) ^ D.region.card := by\n   511\t  rw [← trace_regionToQubitMatrix, regionToQubitMatrix_regionProjector]\n   512\t  exact D.stabilizerData.stabilizerProjector_trace\n   513\t\n   514\t/-- The local density matrix has trace one. -/\n   515\ttheorem regionDensity_trace : D.regionDensity.trace = 1 := by\n   516\t  rw [← trace_regionToQubitMatrix, regionToQubitMatrix_regionDensity]\n   517\t  exact D.stabilizerData.stabilizerDensity_trace\n   518\t\n   519\t/-- The local density matrix is the trace-normalized local code projector. -/\n   520\ttheorem regionDensity_eq_trace_normalized_regionProjector :\n   521\t    D.regionDensity = (D.regionProjector.trace)⁻¹ • D.regionProjector := by\n   522\t  apply (regionToQubitMatrix D.region).injective\n   523\t  rw [regionToQubitMatrix_regionDensity, map_smul,\n   524\t    regionToQubitMatrix_regionProjector, ← trace_regionToQubitMatrix,\n   525\t    regionToQubitMatrix_regionProjector]\n   526\t  exact D.stabilizerData.stabilizerDensity_eq_trace_normalized_projector\n   527\t\n   528\t/-- The local density matrix is positive semidefinite. -/\n   529\ttheorem regionDensity_posSemidef : D.regionDensity.PosSemidef := by\n   530\t  rw [← submatrix_regionToQubitMatrix D.region D.regionDensity,\n   531\t    regionToQubitMatrix_regionDensity]\n   532\t  exact (Matrix.posSemidef_submatrix_equiv (regionBasisEquiv D.region).symm).mpr\n   533\t    D.stabilizerData.stabilizerDensity_posSemidef\n   534\t\n   535\t/-- The local code projector is positive semidefinite and nonzero. -/\n   536\ttheorem regionProjector_ne_zero : D.regionProjector ≠ 0 := by\n   537\t  intro hzero\n   538\t  refine D.stabilizerData.stabilizerProjector_ne_zero ?_\n   539\t  rw [← regionToQubitMatrix_regionProjector, hzero, map_zero]\n   540\t\n   541\tend FullPauliRegionStabilizer\n   542\t\n   543\t/-! ### Non-vacuity: explicit finite consistent stabilizer subgroups -/\n   544\t\n   545\t/-- The two-element subgroup generated by an involutive full Pauli word. -/\n   645\trealizability inside the local matrix algebra of `F`.\n   646\t-/\n   647\tnoncomputable def localStabilizerSubgroup (S : Subgroup (FullPauliWord Site))\n   648\t    (F : Finset Site) : Subgroup (FullPauliWord Site) :=\n   649\t  S ⊓ FullPauliWord.localGroup F\n   650\t\n   651\ttheorem mem_localStabilizerSubgroup_iff (S : Subgroup (FullPauliWord Site))\n   652\t    (F : Finset Site) (a : FullPauliWord Site) :\n   653\t    a ∈ localStabilizerSubgroup S F ↔ a ∈ S ∧ a.label.support ⊆ F :=\n   654\t  Subgroup.mem_inf\n   655\t\n   656\t/-- The local stabilizer group of a finite region is finite, with no assumption on `S`. -/\n   657\tnoncomputable def localStabilizerSubgroupFintype (S : Subgroup (FullPauliWord Site))\n   658\t    (F : Finset Site) : Fintype ↥(localStabilizerSubgroup S F) := by\n   659\t  letI : Fintype ↥(FullPauliWord.localGroup F) := FullPauliWord.localGroupFintype F\n   660\t  have hinj : Function.Injective\n   661\t      (fun g : ↥(localStabilizerSubgroup S F) =>\n   662\t        (⟨g.1, ((mem_localStabilizerSubgroup_iff S F g.1).mp g.2).2⟩ :\n   663\t          ↥(FullPauliWord.localGroup F))) := by\n   664\t    intro g h hgh\n   665\t    exact Subtype.ext (congrArg (fun x : ↥(FullPauliWord.localGroup F) =>\n   666\t      (x : FullPauliWord Site)) hgh)\n   667\t  have : Finite ↥(localStabilizerSubgroup S F) := Finite.of_injective _ hinj\n   668\t  exact Fintype.ofFinite _\n   669\t\n   670\t/--\n   671\t**The manuscript's local stabilizer data.**  A global consistent stabilizer\n   672\tsubgroup of `FullPauliWord Site`, all of whose elements are involutive,\n   673\trestricts to an explicitly finite consistent stabilizer subgroup in every\n   674\tfinite region.  No countability, exhaustion, or long-range-order input is\n   675\tused: finiteness of the local group is proved from finite support alone.\n   676\t-/\n   677\tnoncomputable def FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGlobalStabilizer\n   678\t    (S : Subgroup (FullPauliWord Site)) (F : Finset Site)\n   679\t    (hinv : ∀ g ∈ S, g * g = 1)\n   680\t    (hcons : FullPauliWord.negativeIdentity (Site := Site) ∉ S) :\n   681\t    FullPauliRegionStabilizer Site where\n   682\t  group := localStabilizerSubgroup S F\n   683\t  region := F\n   684\t  groupFintype := localStabilizerSubgroupFintype S F\n   685\t  supported g hg := ((mem_localStabilizerSubgroup_iff S F g).mp hg).2\n   686\t  involutive g hg := hinv g ((mem_localStabilizerSubgroup_iff S F g).mp hg).1\n   687\t  consistent hmem :=\n   688\t    hcons ((mem_localStabilizerSubgroup_iff S F _).mp hmem).1\n   689\t\n   690\t/--\n   691\tThe manuscript's actual input: a set of pairwise-commuting order-two full\n   692\tPauli generators whose generated group excludes `-1` gives, in every finite\n   693\tregion, an explicitly finite consistent stabilizer subgroup.\n   694\t-/\n   695\tnoncomputable def FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGenerators\n   696\t    (G : FullPauliWord.StabilizerGeneratorData Site) (F : Finset Site) :\n   697\t    FullPauliRegionStabilizer Site :=\n   698\t  FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGlobalStabilizer (Subgroup.closure G.generators) F\n   699\t    (fun g hg => G.closure_involutive g hg) G.no_negative_identity\n   700\t\n   701\t/--\n   702\t**The manuscript's finite-volume density for a generated stabilizer system.**\n   703\tFor pairwise-commuting order-two full Pauli generators whose group excludes\n   704\t`-1`, and for any finite region `F`, the group average\n   705\t`ρ_F = 2^{-|F|} ∑_{g ∈ G_{S,F}} g` of the finite-region matrix images is a\n   706\tpositive semidefinite matrix of trace one, equal to the trace-normalized local\n   707\tcode projector.\n   708\t-/\n   709\ttheorem regionDensity_ofGenerators\n   710\t    (G : FullPauliWord.StabilizerGeneratorData Site) (F : Finset Site) :\n   711\t    (FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGenerators G F).regionDensity.PosSemidef ∧\n   712\t      (FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGenerators G F).regionDensity.trace = 1 ∧\n   713\t      (FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGenerators G F).regionDensity =\n   714\t        ((FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGenerators G F).regionProjector.trace)⁻¹ •\n   715\t          (FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGenerators G F).regionProjector :=\n   716\t  ⟨(FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGenerators G F).regionDensity_posSemidef,\n   717\t    (FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGenerators G F).regionDensity_trace,\n   718\t    (FullPauliRegionStabilizer.ofGenerators G F).regionDensity_eq_trace_normalized_regionProjector⟩\n   719\t\n   720\t/-- The one-site `Z` word: trivial central phase, projective label `(0,1)` at `s`. -/\n   106\t- when the user requested a “handsoff file” and current-status documentation -> leave durable resume artifacts with exact checked/open boundaries rather than relying on chat context [Task 2]\n   107\t\n   108\t## Reusable knowledge\n   109\t\n   110\t- The live theorem is `writing/overleaf_prl_stabilizer_region_algebras/main.tex:1501` (`thm:finite_projections_exist`): every nonzero central projection `z` has a finite nonzero projection in `zM_Γ`. The stronger reusable target is `full_tracial_corner_semifinite`: a faithful tracial corner `qMq` plus full `q` implies each nonzero central summand contains a finite nonzero projection; finite central fibers/sectors are a corollary, not finite-dimensional fibers. [Task 1]\n   111\t- Use the standalone `formalization_finite_fibers/` package, preserving `work/OLD/formalization/`. Its old `VNTrace` interface is too weak for complex-linear trace subtraction such as `τ(q - vv*) = 0`. [Task 1]\n   112\t- `FiniteFiber/CountablePauliRepresentation.lean` realizes `K := ℕ →₀ ZMod 2` and `H := Lp ℂ 2 (Measure.count)`, with translations and bounded phase multipliers. Lp action formulas are almost-everywhere (`=ᵐ[Measure.count]`): translations use `MeasureTheory.measurePreserving_add_left` and `MeasureTheory.Lp.compMeasurePreservingₗᵢ`; phase multiplication uses an L∞ certificate and `ContinuousLinearMap.holderL`. [Task 2]\n   113\t- Verify with focused and full `lake build`, `lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean`, direct theorem audits, and the handoff. Checked declarations used only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`; both independent reviews were APPROVED. [Task 2]\n   114\t- The next local step is shift composition, then involution/operator Pauli relations; the larger bridge remains finite/tail factorization and faithful finite local matrix images. [Task 2]\n   115\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: history/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF17-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md\n+# FF17 live closeout — full-Pauli stabilizer density\n+\n+**Decision: ACCEPTED at the packet's stated finite-volume scope.**\n+\n+## Quarantine and integration\n+\n+- Aristotle project: \"'`a8623a7e-5752-4e4d-9667-d3c741247c1f`; completed task:\n+  `44158f6b-4673-4e26-9871-9fc7717c0353`.\n+- Raw archive retained at `FF17-full-pauli-stabilizer-density.tar.gz`, SHA-256\n+  `7e86f988e2118b9e43141f319f65b9ccf5ae0802be34147d670212acdfc84a63`.\n+- Complete dependency-free snapshot retained under `FF17-extracted/`; no Lake\n+  command was run there.\n+- Integrated only `FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean`.  Its live and\n+  quarantined SHA-256 values agree:\n+  `688162cc2779855e163f45fd210e4ddd36339579136fd3039f19df82cfca0a09`.\n+- Rejected: the remote README attribution block, `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md`,\n+  source-context/autonomy metadata, and the remote `manuscript/` copy.  No\n+  manuscript or root import file was modified.\n+\n+## Proved\n+\n+For `D : FullPauliRegionStabilizer Site`, the exact hypotheses are the fields\n+at `FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean:303`: a subgroup of\n+`FullPauliWord Site`, a finite `region`, an explicit `Fintype` on the subgroup,\n+support containment for every group member, elementwise involutivity\n+`g * g = 1`, and exclusion of `FullPauliWord.negativeIdentity`.\n+\n+- `FullPauliRegionStabilizer.stabilizerData` constructs\n+  `FinitePauliStabilizerData D.group D.region.card`; the representation\n+  injectivity and matrix `-1` exclusion are established internally, rather\n+  than inserted as fields.\n+- The packet'\"'s target identity is exactly\n+  \"'`FullPauliRegionStabilizer.regionToQubitMatrix_regionDensity`\n+  (`FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean:477`): after the explicit basis\n+  reindexing, the finite-region average\n+  `((2 : C)''^D.region.card)''^(-1) * sum_g fullPauliRegionMatrix D.region g`\n+  is `D.stabilizerData.stabilizerDensity`.\n+- The exact normal-form convention is preserved by\n+  `fullPauliRegionMatrix_eq_pauliSign_smul`: the central `ZMod 4` phase plus\n+  the checked Hermitian correction produces the signed Pauli term used by the\n+  finite-density layer.\n+- Derived finite-volume conclusions are checked: projector invariance,\n+  self-adjoint idempotence, trace formula, trace-one density,\n+  trace-normalized-projector identity, positive semidefiniteness, and nonzero\n+  projector (`:490`--`:539`).\n+- `ofGlobalStabilizer` retains the added premises explicitly:\n+  `hinv : forall g in S, g * g = 1` and `negativeIdentity notin S` (`:677`--`:688`).\n+  `ofGenerators` discharges these only from the existing explicit\n+  pairwise-commuting, order-two, consistent generator data; it does not infer\n+  them from short-range order.\n+\n+## Partial\n+\n+This accepts only the manuscript'\"'s finite-region density formula\n+\"'`rho_F = 2''^(-|F|) sum_{g in G_{S,F}} g` and its finite matrix consequences.\n+The module does not prove region-to-region partial-trace compatibility, a\n+quasilocal completion, a global state, GNS data, normality, or a finite-fiber/\n+type conclusion.  Those remain open and are not needed for FF17.\n+\n+## Blocked\n+\n+None within the stated FF17 target.\n+\n+## Failed\n+\n+None.  No target was silently weakened: the finite group, its support,\n+involutivity, and consistency are all visible assumptions of the proved\n+finite-volume theorem.\n+\n+## Adversarial review\n+\n+No confirmed defect found.  The main potential scope failure—treating a\n+finite syntactic local group as a completed quasilocal construction—is avoided:\n+the only global-group constructor remains conditional and the source explicitly\n+disclaims every global-state/GNS claim.  The matrix identity is transported by\n+an explicit basis algebra equivalence, not asserted by notation.\n+\n+## Live verification\n+\n+All commands below were run in `formalization_finite_fibers`, never in the\n+quarantine snapshot:\n+\n+```text\n+lake build FiniteFiber.FullPauliStabilizerDensity                PASS\n+lake build FiniteFiber.FinitePauliStabilizer                     PASS\n+lake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication      PASS\n+lake build FiniteFiber.FullPauliSupportLocality                  PASS\n+lake build FiniteFiber                                           PASS\n+lake build                                                       PASS\n+lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean                              PASS\n+```\n+\n+A direct generated `#print axioms` audit covered all 41 public FF17 theorems.\n+Each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.  A direct\n+scan found no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, or\n+`implemented_by` token in the new module.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n\ngit status --short -- FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF17-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
